statement:
Fix $p > 0$, let $f : \{0,1\}^{n+1} \to \bbr$ be a Boolean function, and let $x' \in \{0,1\}^n$. Writing $(x', b) \in \{0,1\}^{n+1}$ for the point obtained by appending a bit $b \in \{0,1\}$ to $x'$, and taking the expectation over the single free bit under the uniform measure, one has
\[
  \Bigl(\E_{b \in \{0,1\}}\bigl[\,\abs{f(x', b)}^p\,\bigr]\Bigr)^{1/p}
  \;=\;
  \left(\frac{\abs{f(x', 0)}^p + \abs{f(x', 1)}^p}{2}\right)^{1/p}.
\]
